>

  <!-- WHY WE BUILT IT -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="The Problem" heading="Why We Built It">
    <p>A missed call rarely gets a second try. For a small or solo business, answering every call while working a job or with a client isn't realistic — and the caller usually just moves on to the next name on the list. Reception was built to close that gap: when a call goes unanswered, the caller gets an immediate WhatsApp reply, so at least they know they were seen and know what to do next.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!-- WHAT IT DOES -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="The Solution" heading="What It Does" accent="gold">
    <p>The moment a business misses a call, Reception sends an automatic WhatsApp message from that business's own number — not a shared or generic number, so it reads to the caller as a real reply from the business, not a bot from somewhere else. It was built as a bilingual product, in English and Hebrew, with a demo built specifically so a visitor could feel exactly what their own missed callers would receive.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!-- HOW IT'S BUILT -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="Architecture" heading="How It's Built">
    <p>A simple, deliberately small architecture: a lead-capture form protected by an invisible bot check, submitting into a background workflow that handles everything past that point — keeping the moving parts to a minimum for a product built this narrow.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!--
